# Unicode CLDR, cldr-json cldr-dates-full/main/ha/dateFields.json.
# Every past relativeTime pattern is the unit, the count, and a trailing
# relative clause: "kwanaki {0} da suka gabata", "wata {0} da ya gabata",
# "shekara {0} da ta gabata".  The verb agrees with the unit noun -- ya for
# masculine, ta for feminine, suka for the plural -- so all three ship: which
# one is grammatical was settled by the noun the writer already chose.
# CLDR gives wuce beside gabata for Friday and Saturday; the two verbs are
# interchangeable in the frame and both ship.
da ya gabata
da ta gabata
da suka gabata
da ya wuce
da ta wuce
da suka wuce
